# Docker build context exclusions. Must live at the REPO ROOT — the build
# context is the root (see deploy/Dockerfile), and Docker reads .dockerignore
# only from the context root. A copy inside deploy/ is silently ignored.
#
# Without this file the build context is 5.3 GB: the 1.1 GB chatbot/.venv, the
# frontend, and chatbot/.env (which holds a live ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) all get
# baked into the image. Docker does NOT read .gitignore.

.git
.github
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets. The key belongs in Secrets Manager, injected as a runtime env var
# by App Runner — never in an image layer. Layers survive deletion of the file
# in a later step and are readable by anyone who can pull the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

frontend/
data-preprocessing/
pipeline/output/
pipeline/deployment/
proto/
tools/

# **/ not just *: .dockerignore patterns are root-relative, so a bare *.md
# leaves chatbot/README.md (57 KB) in the context.
**/*.md
**/*.png

chatbot/cache/*.partial
chatbot/test_*.py
chatbot/this_script.py
chatbot/check_key.py

# NOT excluded, deliberately: chatbot/chat.html (22 KB).
# main.py registers two routes that read it from disk at REQUEST time —
# GET /standalone always, and GET / as a fallback when no frontend build is
# mounted (which is the production case here). Excluding it makes both routes
# raise FileNotFoundError -> HTTP 500. 22 KB is worth keeping for a
# self-contained smoke-test page that needs no frontend build.
